# Every text file is committed and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# The CLI's tests compare bytes: the embedded template against the tree it was
# packed from, a rename against the file it rewrote, `docs/flows` against a
# fresh export. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` — the runner's
# default — would rewrite every one of those to CRLF and fail all of them for
# a reason that has nothing to do with frx. Stated here rather than in a
# runner setting, because a contributor's own clone has the same default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary by extension, so the heuristic never has to guess about one.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.jar binary
*.vsix binary
